api.procedure:
1. PATCH /auth/me {"full_name":"QA Updated"}
2. GET /auth/me.
3. PATCH /auth/me {"email":"other@example.com"}

1. GET /creators/me/organization.
2. PATCH /creators/me/organization {"name":"QA Org","organization_type":"nonprofit"}
3. PATCH /creators/me/organization {"city":"Calgary"}
4. GET /creators/me/organization.

1. GET /applications/received?status=pending&opportunity_id={opp_id}.
2. POST /applications/{a}/decision {"decision":"accepted"}
3. POST /applications/{b}/decision {"decision":"rejected"}
4. Repeat decision on {a}.

1. GET /submissions/received?status=awaiting.
2. POST /submissions/{id}/verification {"decision":"approved","verified_hours":"5"}
3. GET /contributors/me/experience as applicant.

1. POST verification with {"decision":"rejected"}
2. POST verification with {"decision":"rejected","comment":"Incomplete evidence"}
3. GET /contributors/me/experience as applicant.

1. POST /applications/{id}/feedback as contributor {"rating":5,"reports_discrepancy":true}
2. POST same endpoint as creator {"rating":1}
3. GET /applications/{id}/feedback as each participant.

1. POST /admin/feedback/{id}/review {"decision":"rejected"}
2. POST review {"decision":"rejected","reason":"Inappropriate comment"}
3. GET public rating; GET feedback as recipient.

1. POST /opportunities/{id}/reports {"reason":"unsafe_conditions","details":"QA private detail"}
2. GET /reports/mine.
3. Repeat POST for same opportunity.

1. POST /admin/reports/{id}/review {"decision":"upheld"}
2. POST review {"decision":"upheld","reason":"Safety concern confirmed"}
3. GET /admin/reports?opportunity_id={opp_id}; GET /opportunities/{opp_id}.
4. GET /opportunities/{opp_id}/takedown as owning creator.

1. POST /admin/reports/{id}/review {"decision":"upheld","reason":"QA"}
2. POST review {"decision":"dismissed"}
3. GET opportunity.

1. POST /opportunities/{id}/close as owner.
2. POST /opportunities/{opp_id}/applications as contributor, multipart application_details as JSON object of strings, optional motivation.
3. POST existing pending application decision as owner {"decision":"accepted"}

1. POST /opportunities/{id}/cancel.
2. POST /applications/{id}/decision {"decision":"accepted"}
3. GET opportunity and pending application.

1. GET /notifications with the intended recipients' and unrelated users' tokens; record existing notification IDs.
2. POST /applications/{id}/feedback {"rating":5,"reports_discrepancy":true}
3. Poll GET /notifications for each recipient and unrelated control user for up to 60 seconds. Record new notification IDs and content for this test record.

1. GET /notifications with the intended recipients' and unrelated users' tokens; record existing notification IDs.
2. POST /opportunities/{id}/reports {"reason":"unsafe_conditions","details":"QA-private"}
3. Poll GET /notifications for each recipient and unrelated control user for up to 60 seconds. Record new notification IDs and content for this test record.

1. GET /notifications with the intended recipients' and unrelated users' tokens; record existing notification IDs.
2. POST /admin/reports/{id}/review {"decision":"upheld","reason":"QA safety"}
3. Poll GET /notifications for each recipient and unrelated control user for up to 60 seconds. Record new notification IDs and content for this test record.

1. GET /notifications with the intended recipients' and unrelated users' tokens; record existing notification IDs.
2. POST /admin/reports/{id}/review {"decision":"dismissed","reason":"QA review"}
3. Poll GET /notifications for each recipient and unrelated control user for up to 60 seconds. Record new notification IDs and content for this test record.
